# Specification authority and hierarchy

## Rule

Distinguish corporate, departmental, and project specifications by **logical scope**, independently of storage location. Authorized corporate rules take precedence over departmental rules, which take precedence over project rules. More-specific documents refine higher-level requirements but MUST NOT silently contradict them.

An authorized exception must be explicitly justified and approved. A `draft` is a proposed rule and is not approved policy solely because it appears in the repository.

## Verification

For any detected contradiction report the document IDs, scope, status and proposed resolution; do not silently choose a winner based on filename or discovery order.
